# Registrations written by `continuum mcp install --host <host> --scope
# project`, one entry per `project_settings` in HOST_PROFILES
# (src/continuum/mcp/install.py). These bake an absolute command and an
# absolute --db resolved on one contributor's machine, so a committed copy
# points every other clone at a binary that cannot start and makes
# `continuum doctor` report the project itself as stale (#1618). `.mcp.json`
# is the deliberate exception: it carries a path expression the host expands
# rather than a resolved path, so it is tracked on purpose and must stay
# unignored. `.vscode/mcp.json` is already covered by `.vscode/` above.
.continue/config.yaml
.cursor/mcp.json
.codex/config.toml
.zed/settings.json
opencode.json

# Generated by examples/crash_recovery_agent.py
# demo-run artifacts are ignored except the regenerable script and its worker
demo-run/*
!demo-run/generate_crash_visual.py
!demo-run/worker.py

# opencode local state
.opencode/

# Benchmark artifacts
benchmarks/out/

# git worktree metadata must never be tracked: a committed worktree
# registers as a gitlink with no .gitmodules entry, which breaks
# any `git submodule` walk for every consumer of this repo.
.worktrees/
